(
    title: "BASIC Programming",
    developer: Some("Warren Robinett"),
    description: Some("Atari\'s most literal \"Game Program\": a cartridge for writing and running your own programs in a stripped-down BASIC, typed in on the two keypad controllers. The screen splits into windows for the program, the stack, output, variables and graphics; a program can hold only a handful of statements, but you can move a ball around, do arithmetic and watch the machine execute your code. Written by Warren Robinett, who went on to make Adventure."),
